  "draft_py": "# Refute: \"Counter target spell. Draw a card, then discard a card.\"\n# Sentence 1 is the compiler's COUNTER_SPELL (B5a-counter-spell), kept. Sentence 2 is the exact\n# sentence's parse in an activated frame (B3-seq-draw-discard, M21 Obsessive Stitcher, verified):\n# DRAW 1, then a MOVE_ZONE of one card you choose from your hand to your graveyard.\ncounter = compiled[0].effect\ndraw = A(Verb.DRAW, {'amount': QConst(value=1), 'controller': ControllerRef.YOU})\ndiscard = A(Verb.MOVE_ZONE, {\n    'cards': Selector(\n        count=QConst(value=1),\n        mode=SelectorMode.CHOOSE,\n        filter=FAnd(children=()),\n        zones=(Zone(kind=ZoneKind.HAND, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),),\n    ),\n    'controller': ControllerRef.YOU,\n    'destination': Zone(kind=ZoneKind.GRAVEYARD, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),\n    'from': Zone(kind=ZoneKind.HAND, controller=ControllerRef.YOU),\n})\nabilities = [SpellAbility(kind=SpellKind.INSTANT, effect=Seq(steps=(counter, draw, discard)))]\n",
